Deploy:
npm run deploy

That builds the app and pushes the dist/ folder to a gh-pages branch automatically. Then go to your repo → Settings → Pages → Source → Deploy from
branch → gh-pages. Your app will be live at https://YOUR_USERNAME.github.io/YOUR_REPO/.

Every time you want to update the live site, just run npm run deploy again.

---

How sharing works:

1. You add apartments, click Export → downloads nyc-apartments-2026-05-05.json
2. Send the file to your friend (AirDrop, iMessage, email, whatever)
3. They open the same GitHub Pages URL, click Import, pick the file
4. Import is merge-based — it only adds apartments they don't already have, so running it twice won't create duplicates

